      "hardware_label": "2x RTX 3090 24GB",
      "notes": "Lenovo ThinkStation P620 (TR Pro 5955WX, 64 GB DDR4-3200 ECC), 2x RTX 3090 (1x Gigabyte Waterforce Xtreme 3090 Ti + 1x NVIDIA Founders Edition 3090), both PCIe Gen4 x16, both 250 W power cap, ReBAR enabled (BAR1 32 GB each), no NVLink, NODE topology (GPU0 domain 40, GPU1 domain 60). Engine: vLLM 0.20.2 + torch 2.11.0 + CUDA 13.x runtime. Marlin FP8 dequant (Ampere has no native FP8 tensor cores). TP=2 across both cards via NCCL allreduce. MTP n=3 speculative decoding via Qwen-shipped mtp.safetensors weights, acceptance 56.12% (per-position 70.19/54.82/43.35), accept length 2.68. Methodology: vllm bench serve, random 512in/512out, 20 prompts, max-concurrency 1, --save-result. Hardware-delta context: bench-paired no-MTP run on same rig was 44.82 t/s, vs prior PC dual-3090 vLLM FP8 entry at 44.17 t/s (+1.5%, within noise) - confirming PCIe x16 vs x4 contributes ~zero to single-stream throughput. The +75% MTP uplift is all software, not hardware.",
